WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.569
This page explains how business systems can use evidence without reading PDF files.

2
00:00:05.519 --> 00:00:16.639
The API model lets authorised users request quotes, submit batch records, read verification status, request public time anchors and export registry information.

3
00:00:16.639 --> 00:00:22.264
Each resource has a defined path and purpose, making integration easier to review.

4
00:00:22.264 --> 00:00:32.498
Security is separated from access: an API key controls submission, while public commitments and timestamps let anyone check a published record.

5
00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:35.623
Even a leaked key must not rewrite history.

6
00:00:35.623 --> 00:00:45.675
Teams can begin with one real workflow, map identifiers and evidence gaps, and agree how failures should be handled before building an integration.
